# Nine-point circle: Euler points — the midpoint of AH lies on the circle through the three side midpoints (source: Johnson, Advanced Euclidean Geometry)
A B C = triangle
H = orthocenter(A, B, C)
Ma = midpoint(B, C)
Mb = midpoint(C, A)
Mc = midpoint(A, B)
Ea = midpoint(A, H)
prove cyclic(Ma, Mb, Mc, Ea)
